e gracefully. If not, consider increasing the timeout or implementing a more robust termination strategy.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java--5236:5294","promptId":"#T8ATK","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5236,"endPos":5294,"startLine":131,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":131,"endLineOffset":70,"length":59}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":99,"line":99,"comment_lines":["[][99]"],"review_comment":["I don\u0027t think we need a `ScheduledThreadPoolExecutor` here, could we just use a regular `EsThreadPoolExecutor` instead? I\u0027d rather we customized the rejection behaviour by making `ResourceMonitor` an `AbstractRunnable` and overriding its `onRejection`, although I think this would need some changes to `ThreadPool#scheduleWithFixedDelay` too.","Thanks, I\u0027ll take a look at doing that. I wasn\u0027t sure what our best practices are these days for things like this, so I\u0027m definitely open to taking a different tack. I saw the fix, but it\u0027s still causing a bit of log spam due to the long task durations, so I think doing it on a dedicated thread (or at least not blocking a general-use threadpool about it) would be best.","Hmm what log spam are you seeing? I wouldn\u0027t expect any warnings about long-running tasks on `generic`.","I did a very silly thing; when I checked that this was still a problem... I did not filter the logs by version. If I filter out versions below 8.9.0 (where the fix you reference was released), there is no log spam. I\u0027m going to blame it on getting too used to serverless logs and everything being a very current version all the time. I think I\u0027m just going to close this (and the referenced issue) as I don\u0027t think there\u0027s enough of a problem remaining to justify more effort in the short term; apologies for the noise."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java","id":36598,"created_at":"2024-09-12T04:19:43Z","original_position":50,"side":"RIGHT","position":50,"submitted_on_commit":"8c58585ee9dcd3b04fc93e07f7aeb93791ca0c3c","diff_hunk":"@@ -75,32 +76,49 @@ public enum Frequency {\n \n     private final boolean enabled;\n \n+    private final Scheduler.SafeScheduledThreadPoolExecutor executor;\n+\n     final ResourceMonitor lowMonitor;\n     final ResourceMonitor mediumMonitor;\n     final ResourceMonitor highMonitor;\n \n-    private final Cancellable lowFuture;\n-    private final Cancellable mediumFuture;\n-    private final Cancellable highFuture;\n+    private final Scheduler.Cancellable lowFuture;\n+    private final Scheduler.Cancellable mediumFuture;\n+    private final Scheduler.Cancellable highFuture;\n \n     public ResourceWatcherService(Settings settings, ThreadPool threadPool) {\n         this.enabled \u003d ENABLED.get(settings);\n \n-        TimeValue interval \u003d RELOAD_INTERVAL_LOW.get(settings);\n-        lowMonitor \u003d new ResourceMonitor(interval, Frequency.LOW);\n-        interval \u003d RELOAD_INTERVAL_MEDIUM.get(settings);\n-        mediumMonitor \u003d new ResourceMonitor(interval, Frequency.MEDIUM);\n-        interval \u003d RELOAD_INTERVAL_HIGH.get(settings);\n-        highMonitor \u003d new ResourceMonitor(interval, Frequency.HIGH);\n         if (enabled) {\n-            final var executor \u003d threadPool.generic();\n+            TimeValue interval \u003d RELOAD_INTERVAL_LOW.get(settings);\n+            lowMonitor \u003d new ResourceMonitor(interval, Frequency.LOW);\n+            interval \u003d RELOAD_INTERVAL_MEDIUM.get(settings);\n+            mediumMonitor \u003d new ResourceMonitor(interval, Frequency.MEDIUM);\n+            interval \u003d RELOAD_INTERVAL_HIGH.get(settings);\n+            highMonitor \u003d new ResourceMonitor(interval, Frequency.HIGH);\n+            executor \u003d new Scheduler.SafeScheduledThreadPoolExecutor(1, (runnable, exec) -\u003e {","submitted_line":99},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `ResourceMonitor` instances (`lowMonitor`, `mediumMonitor`, `highMonitor`) are initialized inside the `if (enabled)` block and set to null if `enabled` is false. This is fine, but ensure that any code using these monitors checks if they are null before calling methods on them.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java-3255:3310,3319:3377,3386:3434,3443:3507,3516:3562,3571:3631,3667:3709-3409:3464,3477:3535,3548:3596,3609:3673,3686:3732,3745:3805,3818:4488,4836:4854,4867:4888,4901:4920,5027:5043","promptId":"#RE3ED","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/watcher/ResourceWatcherService.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3255,"endPos":3310,"startLine":89,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":89,"endLineOffset":63,"length":56},{"pos":3319,"endPos":3377,"startLine":90,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":90,"endLineOffset":66,"length":59},{"pos":3386,"endPos":3434,"startLine":91,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":91,"endLineOffset":56,"length":49},{"pos":3443,"endPos":3507,"startLine":92,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":92,"endLineOffset":72,"length":65},{"pos":3516,"endPos":3562,"startLine":93,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":93,"endLineOffset":54,"length":47},{"pos":3571,"endPos":3631,"startLine":94,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":94,"endLineOffset":68,"length":61},{"pos":3667,"endPos":3709,"startLine":96,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":96,"endLineOffset":54,"length":43}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3409,"endPos":3464,"startLine":93,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":93,"endLineOffset":67,"length":56},{"pos":3477,"endPos":3535,"s